/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  postDict -- SIZING of the units that are pieces of equipment (DEV.md 4c
  C76), so the plant has design/ sheets and a plot plan can place them
  (system/layoutDict).  SIZING ONLY: there is no costing and no economics
  pass here on purpose -- pricing the plant is part of the students'
  optimisation, and adding one is a `costing {}` block (see
  greenAmmoniaPEQ_baseCase for the shape).

  WHAT IS SIZED, AND ON WHAT BASIS.  Five of the nine units -- one item
  each, and four for the lights column:

    preheater     (phaseChanger)      shellTubeHX, A = Q/(U*LMTD): Q is the
                  unit's own duty, the LMTD is COMPUTED from its own inlet
                  and outlet temperatures (320 -> 460 K) against HP steam
                  (data/standards/utilities/steamHP.dat, 525 K), and U is
                  DECLARED.  This route publishes an AREA, not a shell, so
                  the plot plan gives it a declared box.
    reactor       (gibbsReactor)      vessel on a DECLARED volume.  An
                  equilibrium reactor has no kinetics, so it has no volume
                  of its own; the number below is a HAND CALCULATION on the
                  base case, written out so it can be redone (it does NOT
                  follow the run: change the flowsheet and redo it).
    condenser     (isothermalFlash)   vessel, the knock-out drum, by VAPOUR
                  residence time (V = Q_vapour * tau, ideal gas) -- the
                  greenAmmoniaPEQ_baseCase precedent.  The cooling duty that
                  makes the 330 K is NOT sized as an exchanger: the flowsheet
                  models the condenser as ONE flash, a sizing entry is ONE
                  item per unit, and a cooler sized beside it would need an
                  LMTD typed from temperatures the flash does not publish.
    degasser      (isothermalFlash)   vessel by vapour residence time, the
                  same rule.  READ THIS: the degasser is a LIQUID drum
                  (1.4 % of what enters leaves as vapour), and its size is
                  set by liquid holdup, which this basis does not contain --
                  its volume is a LOWER BOUND, as the PEQ case's let-down
                  drums are.

  THE LIGHTS COLUMN (`type distillationColumn;`) yields FOUR items: the
  shell (a vessel), the tray stack (inside it), the condenser and the
  reboiler (shell-and-tube).  The shell's DIAMETER is the tray-hydraulics
  pass's, in DESIGN mode (the unit's `hydraulics {}` block in
  system/flowsheetDict).  Until 2026-10-17 that pass could not rate these
  trays: their liquid carries a trace of CO and dimethyl ether above their
  critical temperatures, which have no liquid density, and the NaN went
  through every head (design mode refused with a misleading "two downcomers
  leave no active area", rating mode printed "dP -nan" at exit 0 -- found
  during DEV.md 4c C76).  Since DEV.md 4c C79 the trays' liquid density is
  taken over the other components, as the let-down valve's already was, and
  the run SAYS so; a hydraulic number that is not finite refuses by name.
  The column has no reflux drum here (its entry says why).

  WHAT IS NOT SIZED, and why it is not an omission: M1 and M2 are pipe
  junctions, purgeSplit a tee and letdown a control valve -- no vessel, no
  area, no driver -- so no item is invented for them.  Outside the battery
  limit, as the README says: the feed compressor and pump (the feeds are
  declared at 30 bar), the steam, cooling-water and refrigeration systems.

  EVERY DESIGN NUMBER BELOW IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION, declared with its
  reason on its line, for the students to replace with their own design;
  none cites a source because none was read.  The rules they follow:
    * pressureDesign = 1.1 x the highest operating pressure the item sees,
      rounded UP to a whole bar: 33 bar on the 30 bar side, 2 bar on the
      1.5 bar side (the degasser and the lights column);
    * MATERIAL: SS316 on every item, because every one of them touches
      acetic acid hot.  Whether SS316 resists acetic acid at 460 K is NOT
      checked here: the material records carry no corrosion data.  It is the
      students' materials question, and changing it is one word;
    * vessels: a fully radiographed joint (jointEfficiency 1.0), 3 mm of
      corrosion allowance and L/D 3, declared so that no engine default is
      used silently.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

sizing
{
    units
    (
        //  ---- the feed preheater: 320 -> 460 K against HP steam ---------
        { unitName preheater;  type shellTubeHX;  material SS316;
          designRules { utility steamHP;        // 525 K condensing: LMTD computed
                        U 200;                  // W/m2/K, gas film against
                                                // condensing steam -- ASSUMED
                        pressureDesign 33; } }  // 1.1 x 30 bar

        //  ---- the reactor: a vessel on a declared volume ---------------
        //  THE HAND CALCULATION (base case, redo it when the plant moves):
        //    the reactor's liquid is 21.87 mol/s of acetic acid (KPI
        //    N_liq_mol_s) = 1.31 kg/s; at an ASSUMED 850 kg/m3 at 460 K
        //    that is 1.55e-3 m3/s; an ASSUMED 15 min of liquid residence
        //    gives 1.39 m3 of liquid, and an ASSUMED half-full vessel
        //    2.8 m3 -> 3 m3.  A rate law (which this case does not have)
        //    is what would size the reactor; this is a placeholder for it.
        { unitName reactor;  type vessel;  material SS316;
          designRules { volume 3;               // m3 -- the hand calculation above
                        L_over_D 3;  pressureDesign 33;
                        corrosionAllow 0.003;  jointEfficiency 1.0; } }

        //  ---- the drums: vapour residence (see the header) --------------
        { unitName condenser;  type vessel;  material SS316;
          designRules { residenceTime 45;       // s of vapour, a knock-out drum -- ASSUMED
                        flowKey F_beta;  flowUnit kmol/s;     // the vapour leg
                        L_over_D 3;  pressureDesign 33;
                        corrosionAllow 0.003;  jointEfficiency 1.0; } }
        { unitName degasser;   type vessel;  material SS316;
          designRules { residenceTime 60;       // s of vapour -- a LOWER BOUND, see header
                        flowKey F_beta;  flowUnit kmol/s;
                        L_over_D 3;  pressureDesign 2;
                        corrosionAllow 0.003;  jointEfficiency 1.0; } }

        //  ---- the lights column: shell, trays, condenser, reboiler -------
        //  THE DIAMETER IS THE TRAY HYDRAULICS' (the unit's `hydraulics {}`
        //  block in system/flowsheetDict, DESIGN mode); the height is the
        //  tray count times the spacing plus the two end spaces below.
        //  THE TWO LMTDs ARE HAND CALCULATIONS on the base case (redo them
        //  when the plant moves): the condenser at the top-tray temperature
        //  (KPI T_top, 400.7 K) against cooling water 298.15 -> 308.15 K,
        //  LMTD = 10 / ln(102.5/92.5) = 97 K; the reboiler at the bottom
        //  temperature (KPI T_bottom, 404.1 K) against MP steam at 457.2 K
        //  (LP steam, at 400.3 K, is colder than the reboiler and cannot
        //  serve it), LMTD = 53 K.
        //  NO REFLUX DRUM: the drum is sized on the KPI `Q_condensate_m3_s`,
        //  and this column's solver (`model simultaneous;`) does not publish
        //  it -- its stage list carries the condenser as stage 0 with no
        //  vapour, and the KPI is written from that stage's vapour (found
        //  during DEV.md 4c C79, named there, not fixed).  A `refluxDrum {}`
        //  block here would be announced as not built.
        { unitName lightsColumn;  type distillationColumn;  material SS316;
          designRules { traySpacing 0.50;       // m -- the SAME spacing as the
                                                // unit's hydraulics block
                        pressureDesign 2;       // 1.1 x 1.5 bar, rounded up
                        corrosionAllow 0.003;  jointEfficiency 1.0;
                        disengagementHeight 1.2;  // m above the top tray -- ASSUMED
                        sumpHeight 1.5;           // m below the bottom tray -- ASSUMED
                        trayMaterial stainlessSteel;  // the class that prices the
                                                      // trays if a costing pass is added
                        condenser { U 500;      // W/m2/K, condensing vapour against
                                                // water -- ASSUMED
                                    LMTD 97;    // K -- the hand calculation above
                                    pressureDesign 2; }
                        reboiler  { U 800;      // W/m2/K, boiling acid against
                                                // condensing steam -- ASSUMED
                                    LMTD 53;    // K -- the hand calculation above
                                    pressureDesign 2; } } }
    );
}

